From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:14:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] ipa: libipa: af: Support the autofocus controls

AfAlgorithm always runs a continuous autofocus. Add the AfMode,
AfTrigger, AfPause and LensPosition controls, and report the AfState and
AfPauseState, so that an IPA can offer the autofocus controls:

- AfModeManual moves the lens to the LensPosition only;
- AfModeAuto scans once on AfTriggerStart, and AfTriggerCancel stops the
  scan;
- AfModeContinuous, still the default, scans and rescans when the focus
  is lost, and AfPause pauses it, immediately or after the scan.

LensPosition is in dioptres. An optional piecewise linear map in the
tuning data converts it to lens units, and also limits the scans to the
part of the lens range it covers; by default the lens range covers 0 to
10 dioptres. The other constants become optional tuning parameters, with
their current values as defaults: coarse-step, fine-step, max-change and
skip-frames.

While at it, fix a few things in the scan, which change the IPU3
behaviour a little:

- the fine scan used the variance of the last coarse step for its first
  step, and covered the range just below the coarse result rather than
  around it: run it on the next frame, a coarse step either side;
- the scan kept the last position within 10% of the maximum rather than
  the maximum, and could set a lens position past the lens maximum;
- the out-of-focus check truncated the variance change to an integer,
  so a variance below 1 never lost focus, and divided by zero after a
  scan with no contrast;
- a new scan could start on the first out-of-focus frame after a scan,
  as the frames to skip were only counted after an in-focus one.

A scan that finds no contrast at all reports AfStateFailed, and
meteringChanged() lets the IPA start a new continuous scan when the
measured area changes. Add a test for the modes and the tuning.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
